    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s638qwT",
      "title": "Fix `eth_simulateV1` after Jovian fork",
      "author": "kustrun",
      "number": 732,
      "body": "<!--\r\nContributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\r\n-->\r\n\r\nAfter the Jovian fork, all `eth_simulateV1` calls fail with the error: `\"error calculating DA footprint: missing deposit transaction\"`.\r\n\r\nThe root cause is in `CalcDAFootprint()`, which assumes that a deposit transaction exists at `txs[0]` and that it contains the `daFootprintGasScalar` data. This value is required to calculate the rollup gas costs.\r\n\r\nThe proposed solution modifies **ONLY** `eth_simulateV1` by injecting a synthetic Jovian deposit transaction before the user-provided simulation transactions. This allows `CalcDAFootprint()` to succeed while keeping the core block-processing logic unchanged, ensuring that simulations work without affecting normal execution.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2025-12-09T15:39:33Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-01-08T13:34:32Z",
      "additions": 45,
      "deletions": 1
    },
